TTF-27 SplitTryte Core Bank v1.0

Locked core set for TritMux / Netiv / TUI splitTryte text.

[LAYOUT]
splitTryte = [11|OPTIONS|BANK_L|VAL_L2|VAL_L1|VAL_L0|BANK_R|VAL_R2|VAL_R1|VAL_R0]
standard_marker = 11

[DESIGN_RULES]

1. Every splitTryte stores two self-contained symbols.
2. No shift/caps state is required for uppercase/lowercase.
3. BANK:+ is uppercase alphabet plus SPACE.
4. BANK:- is lowercase alphabet plus space.
5. BANK:0 is Netiv/TUI/math numeric-symbol core.
6. ° is core because it is used for degree/angle, top-level TUI bullets, and Netiv syntax.
7. • is core because it is used for point-particles, sub-level TUI bullets, nodes, and Netiv syntax.
8. Full pair table is generated by crossing every left symbol against every right symbol.

[BANK_LANES]

+ = UPPER_ALPHA          = 10

- = LOWER_ALPHA          = 00
  0 = NETIV_NUMERIC_SYMBOL = 01

